% Problem 6. Chace vol. II pl. 38 (photograph X, register 1), PDF pp. 123-124; Peet p. 53 (pl. F).
No. 6
"{The making of loaves 9} for man 10."
"The doing as it occurs."    % Peet: these words "have slipped out of position", standing before "you are to multiply"
Multiply 2/3 '5 '30 by 10.   % "Make thou the multiplication: 2/3 '5 '30 times 10."
  1     2/3 '5 30            % 30 for '30; Chace: fractional dot omitted in the '30 "(twice)"
\ 2     1 2/3 '10 30         % 30 for '30; Chace: fractional dot omitted (second of the two)
  4     3 '2 '10
\ 8     7 '5
Total 9.                     % "Total loaves 9; ..."; Peet's text prints "Total 8 loaves"; Chace fn 2: "By a misprint Peet's text has 8 here. The number is correct on his Plate F."
"it, this is."
